# `docs/*` rather than `docs/`, so a single file can be un-excluded below. Git does not
# descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation under a plain `docs/` would never fire.
docs/*
# The one docs file that ships: the reviewer-facing architecture page the README links to.
# Everything else under docs/ is working material for the build process and stays out.
!docs/architecture.md

